San Andreas

Major Regions and Cities
Los Santos: The main fictional city based on Los Angeles, containing downtown, industrial sectors, and rich neighborhoods.
Blaine County: The northern rural and desert county featuring small towns, mountains, and the Alamo Sea.
North Yankton: A snowy, closed-off prologue and heist location in a different state, accessible via specific replay glitches or missions

Key Neighborhoods & Districts in Los Santos
Vinewood & Vinewood Hills: Modeled after Hollywood, featuring the iconic sign, luxury homes, and the Vinewood Bowl.
Rockford Hills: Based on Beverly Hills, known for high-end shopping and upscale mansions.
Vespucci Beach & Canals: Rendered after Venice Beach, featuring the Del Pero Pier, boardwalk vendors, and gym areas.
Little Seoul: A vibrant commercial district inspired by LA's Koreatown.
Legion Square: A downtown public plaza based on Pershing Square.
South Los Santos / Davis / La Mesa: Denser, industrial, and lower-income neighborhoods.
Los Santos International Airport (LSIA): The major aviation hub occupying the southern coast.

Notable Blaine County Locations
Mount Chiliad: The highest peak in the game, located in the north and popular for off-roading and conspiracy theories.
Alamo Sea: The large inland saltwater lake sitting at the center of Blaine County.
Sandy Shores: A dusty desert town serving as Trevor Philips' base of operations.
Paleto Bay: A small coastal logging and residential town in the northernmost part of the map.
Fort Zancudo: A restricted military base on the western coast housing fighter jets, tanks, and an explorable control tower.
Grapeseed & Harmony: Agricultural and small settlement areas spanning the valleys and deserts.
